# OfxGafferHost: Fix descriptor-handle param lookup (Sapphire)
# Why: Sapphire caches Descriptor* handles from DescribeInContext and reuses them in render-time paramGetValue. Stock HostSupport only registers Instance* and uses reinterpret_cast+verifyMagic to map handle->Instance, so descriptor handles miss and return defaults or kOfxStatFailed (ColorBars etc. also hit fallback). This caused ofx_get_param_internal null handle warnings and default values during S_Blur render.
# Technical: Replace unordered_set<const Instance*> registry with unordered_map<const void*, Instance*> that registers BOTH Instance* and Descriptor* handles to the same Instance*. registerInstance(Instance*, descriptorHandle) maps both, unregisterInstance erases all entries for instance, instanceFromHandle does direct map lookup. Remove defaultFromBase/baseFromHandle fallback, return kOfxStatErrBadHandle for truly unknown handles. Mutex-protected. Sapphire's Show_Blur_Amount HUD and blur render then return actual instance values via getV().
--- a/HostSupport/src/ofxhParam.cpp
+++ b/HostSupport/src/ofxhParam.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
 
+#include <unordered_map>
+#include <mutex>
+
